# Deferred: other-user filter bar shadow on scroll-down

**Status:** Parked. Do not add a always-on shadow under the other-user Items/Outfits filter/sort/search bar unless the user asks.

## Why parked

A static elevation under the bar (matching the other-user bottom bar) was tried and rejected — user does not want it always visible.

## Idea to try later

Show a soft shadow **only after the grid scrolls down** (content moving under the sticky filter bar), and hide it again at scroll top / when the bar is flush with the first row.

## Implementation notes when revisiting

1. Prefer a downward-only shadow that sits on the grid (sticky UIKit chrome clips SwiftUI `.shadow` on the bar itself — upward blur was all that showed).
2. Drive visibility from nested scroll offset in `ProfileNestedScrollContainer` / remote grid (threshold near `contentOffset.y > 0` after header collapse, or equivalent).
3. Match bottom-bar elevation roughly: `opacity ~0.08`, `radius ~8`, cast **under** the bar onto the grid.
4. Remove this rule once shipped or explicitly won’t-do.
